The area of trapezoid $WXYZ$ is $$\frac{1}{2}(12+WX)(WY),$$and our definition of the tangent function is $\tan X = \frac{WY}{ZH}$.  Hence, $WY = HZ \tan X = 12 \tan X = 36$ units.  Similarly, $\tan Z = \frac{H}{ZH}$.  Then, $ZH = \frac{H}{\tan Z} = \frac{4}{3}$ units, so $ZH + YZ = \frac{4}{3} + 12 = \frac{40}{3}$ units, which means that $WX = \frac{2}{3}$ units.

Therefore, our area is $$\frac{1}{2}(12+WX)(WY) = \frac{1}{2}\left(12+\frac{2}{3}\right)(36) = \frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{38}{3}\right)(36)=38(6) = \boxed{228}.$$ </think> <answer> 228 </answer>

